<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_2_2" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_2_2">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_2_2" name="3.2.2 Copper Flotation Circuit" processRef="Process_L3_3_2_2"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_2_2" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>[COPPER-SPECIFIC] Applies to: QB, HVC, Antamina (Cu circuit first), CdA. L0/L1/L2 Process. The Cu flotation circuit selectively recovers chalcopyrite (CuFeS₂) and bornite (Cu₅FeS₄) from the ground slurry into a high-grade Cu concentrate. The circuit typically comprises rougher, scavenger, and cleaner stages in a standard rougher-scavenger-cleaner (RSC) configuration, with regrinding of cleaner tails or scavenger concentrate where liberation is insufficient.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_2_2">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_2_dcs" name="DCS Auto-control">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_2_2_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_2_2_g1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_2_2_g2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_2_2_g3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_2_2_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_2_met" name="Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_2_n1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_2_n2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_2_n3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_2_2_s" name="Conditioned feed at target pH and P80">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_1" name="3.2.2.1 Operate Cu Rougher Flotation">
      <bpmn:documentation>The rougher bank(s) process the full flotation feed and produce a bulk Cu rougher concentrate from the froth overflow. Maximum recovery is the primary objective of the rougher — grade is sacrificed for recovery. Each rougher cell is equipped with a froth scraper or paddled froth crowder; air rate, froth depth, and impeller speed are controlled by DCS per cell. On-stream analysis (XRF) measures feed, concentrate, and tail grades at 2–4 minute intervals. [P754: grade (Cu%, Fe%, S%) | on-stream XRF analyzer | continuous (2–4 min scan interval) | Principles 1, 2, 6, 7 | NO — internal process stream; not a commercial custody transfer point]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: flotation_cell_telemetry, osa_grade_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g1" name="Rougher tail Cu% above threshold?" default="Flow_L3_3_2_2_4">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_2_n1" name="Raise collector dose or cut air rate at scavenger">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_2" name="3.2.2.2 Operate Cu Scavenger Flotation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Scavenger bank(s) process the rougher tailings to maximise recovery of residual Cu minerals. Scavenger concentrate (low grade) is either recycled to the rougher or regrind circuit. Scavenger tailings report to: (a) Cu flotation final tailings at Cu-only sites, or (b) Zn flotation feed at Cu-Zn sequential circuits (Antamina). Additional collector dosing at the scavenger head increases recovery. On-stream analysis monitors scavenger tail grade — this is the Cu recovery loss stream. [P754: grade (Cu% in scavenger tailings — key loss measurement) | on-stream XRF + periodic grab sample | continuous OSA / shift composite | Principles 1, 2, 6, 7 | PARTIAL — scavenger tailings grade at Cu-only sites is the final Cu loss measurement and is material to P754 Principle 7 (verification data)]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g2" name="Scavenger tail Cu% above limit?" default="Flow_L3_3_2_2_8">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_2_n2" name="Investigate feed shift, reagents, OSA calibration; escalate">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_4" name="3.2.2.4 Operate Cu Regrind Mill">
      <bpmn:documentation>Where Cu rougher or scavenger concentrate requires further liberation before cleaning, a regrind mill (typically a stirred media detritor or ball mill) grinds the concentrate to a finer P80 (typically 20–40 µm). Regrind improves cleaner performance by liberating interlocked particles. Not all sites have a dedicated Cu regrind — depends on ore mineralogy and liberation characteristics. [COPPER NOTE: HVC uses regrind for improved Mo circuit feed preparation.]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: regrind_mill_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_3" name="3.2.2.3 Operate Cu Cleaner Flotation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Cleaner bank(s) upgrade the rougher concentrate to final Cu concentrate grade specification (typically 25–35% Cu for smelter contract). Multiple cleaner stages may be used (1st cleaner, 2nd cleaner, sometimes 3rd cleaner). Cleaner tails (low-grade middlings) are recycled to rougher or regrind. Final cleaner concentrate is the Cu product stream — its grade and mass flow are the primary Cu production measurement. [P754: grade (Cu%, Fe%, S%, Au g/t, Ag g/t, Mo% where applicable) + mass flow | on-stream XRF + shift composite sample (lab assay) | continuous OSA + shift composite | Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7 | YES — Cu cleaner final concentrate is a custody transfer point to thickening/dewatering]
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 5, 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (concentrate_production_record — Cu)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g3" name="Grade below smelter spec?" default="Flow_L3_3_2_2_13">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_2_n3" name="Add cleaning stages or adjust froth depth">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_2_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_2_2_e" name="Cu concentrate to thickening">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_2_14</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_2_2_s" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_2" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_1" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_3" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_4" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_5" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_6" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_2" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_7" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_8" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g2" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_9" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_10" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_4" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_11" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_2_3_2_2_3" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_12" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g3" targetRef="End_L3_3_2_2_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_13" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_2_2_g3" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_2_14" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_2_n3" targetRef="End_L3_3_2_2_e"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_2_2">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_2_2" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_2_2">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_2_2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1740" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
